A||N||3||bHooper||a little road racing of my own, today||||1||
Z||000000||bHooper||03-01-2001||02:30 PM||||first, let me introduce the characters:<P>In one corner, a 86 Gt with 2 grown men, totalling 400 lbs, with a 45 lb bag of dog food in the trunk, and a mix mash of toyo 600+4's on the front and some used Generals 65 series on the rear.<P>In the other corner, 2 guys in a mid 20's, driving a "boxy" 3 series BMW, with a torn off air dam.<P>The circuit, tight 40 degree bending fight hander, leading onto a straight, then a side road that meanders through a stop light and into several business parks (with nice wide sweeping roads).<P>All alone, we (GT) took the 40 degree turn at 50 mph and onto the straight, as we approached the left hand turn, i noticed a bmw coming up behind me.  making the turn, and building speed to a steady 65 mph, the bmw was gaining ground.  at the light, it was right behind me, through the light, and the gears it stuck every inch of the way... <P>up ahead, is a wide entrance to an office park, taking the right hand turn in 2nd (~3000 rpms), the bimmer is all over me, riding the tach to 4500 rpms, and a quick left hander.  what?  no distance gained, he's all over me showing himself on the inside! into third gear (briefly), and then down again as we brake for the stop sign.  driving the line into the next park, there he is again... on the inside!  tack it up to about 4000, in 3rd, and i can still see the whites of his eyes!<P>quickly, the office approach's, and letting down the window, i wave... toot, toot, toot... goes the bimmer with no air dam.  <P>another day, my friend... another day.<P>hoping the leprechaun brings me some yoko's for St Patty's day, and a 3.4 for easter!<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000001||firstfiero||03-02-2001||10:43 AM||||   I had an 80 bmw 528i with 200000 miles on it. The way that car handeled I can safely say that my fiero even on it's best day would want no part of it! Unfortunatly it had a rust problem so I got rid of it. My fiero is better looking and more fun anyway.   86se||||reg||7
Z||000002||bHooper||03-02-2001||11:42 AM||||my mom has a '87 528e with about 130,000 miles on it.  she bought it new.  i have always hated that car... one of the most unconfortable things that i have ever driven.<P>but each and every one of us has their favorite car.<P>funny thing about yeasterday, i had though of putting the dog food up front, when i left the store... i wished i had done that.||||reg||1
Z||000003||bHooper||03-02-2001||05:04 PM||||i may have a bit of info on the devil 3 series, from yesterday.<P>there is a BMW repair shop up the street (i already had figurd this fella was involved with it somehow), a coworker of mine is friends with the owner of the shop.  anyway, when i mentioned to him about the little bit of fun we had yesterday, his response was: "oh, i bet the guy had one of Tom's race engines in the car.  he builds, and installs race engines in BMW's all the time."<P>... i now know what must be done.... it ain't pretty, and it ain't cheap, but it has to be done.  <P>hoop||||reg||1
